noC
                noC-LATER v1.21 - (C)1994 nocTurne deSign/Origin
                ------------------------------------------------

                         Synopsis:
                         ---------
                         noC-LATER  provides a graphical means for remote
                         sysops  to boot users off of other nodes, giving
                         them  a  node list through which they can scroll
                         and  select  whom they want to dispose of.  Even
                         those  who  are  transferring files are not free
                         from the wrath of noC-LATER.

    Installation:
    -------------
    Install  noC-LATER  as  you  would  any other /X
    door.   Please note that you must be using v3.38
    or  greater.   The bbscmd icon included requires
    users to have an access of 250 to use the door.

                            Usage:
                            ------
                            After  the  user has typed "LATER" at the prompt
                            and  he  has  sufficient access, a list of users
                            online  and their actions will be displayed.  At
                            that  point  you  may  he  the  cursor  keys  to
                            highlight  the user he wishes to boot, or simply
                            type  the node number.  The user may also update
                            the list by pressing 'U'.  when the desired user
                            is  highlighted, pressing return will bring up a
                            verification  request.   If confirmed, noC-LATER
                            will proceed to knock off the selected user.  It
                            will  take a few moments for the user to be gone
                            completely.

     Credits:
     --------
     noC-LATER  is  a  product  of nocTurne deSign of
     ORiGiN  US  in  1994.   Bug-Reports and comments
